---json
{
  "layout": "layouts/believe.njk",
  "permalink": "/believe/index.html",
  "seo": { "title": "Our principles | Quickler", "description": "Nine principles Quickler stands by: it never makes things up, you sign the report, your layout not ours, and more.", "canonical": "https://quickler.co/believe/" }
}
---
<div class="card">
  <h1 class="site-home-h2" style="font-size:2rem">Our principles.</h1>
  <p class="site-words">Nine principles that shape how Quickler works. Each one is true of the product today.</p>
  {#- Each belief is a Check tile that opens like one in the app (Philip 5 Nov
      2026: "make these drop downs like a check's title would be"). The first
      is open, so a visitor sees what opening one does. -#}
  {%- for b in beliefs %}
  <details class="wf-card site-drop"{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
    <summary class="wf-title-row">
      <span class="wf-name-block"><span class="wf-name">{{ b.title }}</span></span>
      <span class="wf-activity">{{ b.n }}</span>
      <svg class="wf-expand-chevron" width="16" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 7" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 1l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="wf-body site-drop-body">
      <p class="site-words">{{ b.text }}</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
